ra Toriyama for God's sake trunks is  design is based off of John Connor look  at that hair and I don't think I need to  point out that Android 16 looks  strikingly similar to a certain Austrian  film star for now let's take a break  from the 80's and 90's and jump right  back up to the modern day with the  Dragon Ball super in 2017 two characters  were introduced to the world  sentient universe 11 as it's gonna  destruction and it's angel comes Belmont  and margarita immediately it should be  evident that both are references to the  Joker and Harley Quinn from the DC  Batman series sticking with the modern  incarnation let's take a look at one of  the more divisive characters to be  introduced to the series  Kayle Kayle herself is a reference to an  older Dragon Ball character called  growling who actually got his own cannon  appearance this year however that isn't  why Kael has made her way unto this list  it is in fact her reference to the first  Avengers film Kael in her hulking  muscular form while smashing Goku around  is a direct reference to the Hulk and  Loki scene where he gets yeah  flashing backwards from something new to  something old once again we find  ourselves on chapter 71 of the manga  Krillin and lunch are after returning to  Master Roshi's home with some groceries  all seems innocent and normal until you  realize one thing the bag reads Super  Mario which is obviously a reference to  the Super Mario videogame  patio oh here's a fun one did you know  that King Kai's monkey bubbles is named  after a celebrity of sorts or at least  he was a celebrity in the eighties a  celebrity pet a pet that once belonged  to the late Michael Jackson on top of  leading one of the most eccentric lives  perhaps ever owning his own theme park  and zoo on his own property he also was  the proud owner of a chimp that went by  the name of bubbles and finally our last  one perhaps the most obscure reference  in all of Dragonball literally a blink  and you miss it moment and boy is this  one nerdy at the 16-minute mark during  Dragon Ball Z episode 22 you might  notice a news helicopter nothing special  about it really it doesn't even make a  reappearance as it is later destroyed by  nappa  what is special about it however is that  serial number on this side of the  aircraft throw that code into Google and  you find that it is a reference to Star  Trek specifically NCC one seven zero one  a is a reference to a shuttlecraft from  the enterprise a I have never seen Star  Trek but there it is these were my  favorite pop-culture references in  Dragon Ball  your favorite if so let me know down  below in the comment section and who  knows I might update this video with the  sequel if I get enough suggestions don't  forget to leave a like or dislike on  this video and if you would like to see  more videos like this one consider  subscribing and turning that  notification on if you want the  subscription tour catch you guys in the  next video thank you so much for  watching
 

